  "equipment_type": "Air handling / energy recovery ventilation unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Nilan Comfort 1200/5000, VPR and VPM commercial ventilation units (including VPM Cleanroom) with the CTS602 controller, HMI350T panel and the built-in Modbus-to-BACnet gateway.",
  "summary": "Nilan's CTS602 controller speaks Modbus; on these commercial units a built-in Schneider spaceLYnk gateway serves a selected set of registers as a BACnet IP server. The BMS can switch the unit on and off, choose the operating mode and ventilation step, write the room temperature setpoint and cooling, supply-air limit, humidity and CO2 settings, reset alarms and edit the week program. It reads temperatures, pressures, humidity, CO2, fan speeds, relay outputs, digital inputs and the three most recent alarms.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "CTS602 software 1.6.21.0 (Modbus list version 22)",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The object instance is the number in the '#' column (2305-2582); the manual gives the BACnet type as '2 (AV)' or '5 (BV)'.",
    "Square brackets list the unit families marked for a point when it does not apply to all of Comfort, VPR and VPM; T2_Inlet has no family marked.",
    "Alarm dates and times are 16-bit words packed in DOS date/time format.",
    "Control.ModeSet value 4 (Service) is read-only; the manual says to write Modbus register 1005 instead.",
    "Disable the spaceLYnk KNX connection and always answer No to its KNX error box, or several gateways can overwrite each other's setup.",
    "Source: Register layout, sections 4.1-4.13, pages 9-16 (121 objects)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Nilan CTS602 w. HMI350T BACnet - BACnet Protocol, Version 2",
